  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 375 F. Bring a large pot of water to a boil and stir in 1 tbsp salt.",
    "Boil the shells for 8 minutes, until bendy but still firm. Drain and spread them on a tray so they do not stick.",
    "Squeeze the spinach in a clean towel until very dry. Chop it finely so no long strands remain.",
    "In a large bowl, mix the spinach, ricotta, 1 cup mozzarella, Parmesan, egg, 1/2 tsp salt, pepper, and nutmeg until smooth.",
    "Spread 1 cup of marinara over the bottom of a 9 by 13 inch baking dish.",
    "Spoon about 2 tablespoons of filling into each shell. Set the shells open side up in the dish.",
    "Pour the remaining marinara over and around the shells. Sprinkle with the remaining 1 cup mozzarella.",
    "Cover with foil and bake 20 minutes. Uncover and bake 10 to 15 minutes more, until the cheese is melted and golden and the sauce bubbles at the edges.",
    "Rest 5 minutes before serving. To freeze, cool fully, wrap tightly, and reheat covered at 350 F until hot in the center."
  ],
